# Copy to `.env` (git-ignored via root .gitignore `.env*` pattern) and fill in.
#
# GITHUB_PAT: fine-grained Personal Access Token with `Administration: write`
# on this repo only. Generate at:
#   https://github.com/settings/personal-access-tokens/new
#
# Configure the token with:
# - Resource owner: your GitHub account
# - Repository access: Only select repositories → Scone-Willow-Tree-Hotel
# - Repository permissions: Administration → Read and write
# - Expiration: 90 days (rotate on expiry)
#
# Do NOT use a classic PAT with `repo` scope — that grants full repo access
# and is overprivileged for this use case.
GITHUB_PAT=github_pat_replace_me
